  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on identifying a favorable outcome (interpreted here as 'not losing anything', i.e., 0 Euros) and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of achieving it. Lottery B has a 20% chance of this outcome, while Lottery A has 0%. The individual in the verbal report explicitly mentions the 'Chance gar nichts zu verlieren' (chance of not losing anything) as a relevant consideration, indicating that they are attending to the probability of the favorable outcome. Although the individual also notes the higher loss in Lottery B, their justification emphasizes the presence of a chance to avoid loss, which aligns with the core logic of the decision reason—favoring the option with a non-zero probability of the best (or most favorable) outcome, even if other outcomes are worse. The reason's assumption that outcome differences are negligible is not explicitly stated by the individual, but their focus on the possibility of zero loss—rather than a detailed comparison of loss magnitudes—suggests that they are treating the outcome differences as secondary to the chance of avoiding loss. Therefore, the information considered and the justification align closely with the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

